# T46/W-D review fold (A2, lens-1 F1): the repo's first .gitignore.
#
# bridge-lane.jsonl — the cc bridge's STANDALONE default lane log (worker/
# cc-bridge.mjs falls back to <cwd>/bridge-lane.jsonl when BRIDGE_LANE_LOG is
# unset). The file was committed once as pure gate residue and every gate run
# appended to it (the dirty-worktree generator inside the repo's own validate
# gate): untracked now, tests spawn the bridge with BRIDGE_LANE_LOG aimed at
# a tmp path, and this entry keeps any interactive standalone debugging write
# out of git status.
bridge-lane.jsonl
node_modules/
*.log
e2e/out/

# s22/m-10 (the tracked-artifact dirt class): the gates' OWN output reports are
# RUN ARTIFACTS, not source — every drill/stress run rewrites them, so the
# tracked copies made each gate run a dirty worktree (the exact residue class
# bridge-lane.jsonl was). Un-tracked (git rm --cached) in the same fold; the
# durable evidence copies live in the worklog/EVIDENCE discipline, not git.
e2e/last-drill-report.json
stress/last-stress-report.json
